'' A CONVERSION FOLDS ITS ARGUMENT WITH THE SYMBOL TABLE. Every argument of a folded
'' call was evaluated WITHOUT it, so a conversion over a NAMED constant folded to
'' nothing -- 'cbool( FALSE )' and 'cbyte( K )' alike. The constant they initialise
'' then had no value at all, and every USE of it declined rather than the declaration
'' saying so. boolean/boolean-conversions.bas is written out of exactly that shape:
'' 26 declines down to 0.
''
'' The same omission reached IIF's condition and both its arms, and CAST's operand.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/const-conv-fold.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/const-conv-fold.out
